From 8296b73edef5dfec0f3562f5dd61bdda4602a4b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 16:29:48 +0545
Subject: [PATCH] Fix purchase bill flow bugs: cost treatment, duplicates,
 lengths, numbering, due date

- Bill read returns importCostTreatment, so a service bill saved as
  "Landed only" no longer turns back into CIF when it is edited and saved.
- Vendor invoice number is unique per vendor ledger and sub-ledger, and a
  bill that was posted and reversed frees its number, so the supplier's
  invoice can be entered again correctly. The check moves from a unique
  index to the service (migration 0019 swaps it for a lookup index) and is
  serialised with an advisory lock.
- A customs declaration number can be on one live bill of a company only
  (409 naming the bill that holds it).
- Text longer than its column (vendor invoice no. 30, import numbers 30,
  office/bank/transporter 100, country 50) is a 400 naming the field instead
  of a 500; the screen's field widths now match.
- A draft moved into another fiscal year gets that year's next invoice
  number instead of keeping the old year's.
- Screen: due date follows the invoice date and due days.

Tests: five new API tests, a unit test for the date helper, and the
currency test now uses a different declaration number per bill.

